NAME
    gcloud alpha compute hosts - read Compute Engine hosts

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha compute hosts COMMAND [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Read Compute Engine hosts.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     describe
        (ALPHA) Describe a Google Compute Engine host.

     get-version
        (ALPHA) Get software versions for a Compute Engine host.

     list
        (ALPHA) List Google Compute Engine hosts.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

